bundle_api:
EXPORTS (exact, ESM named): schnorrSign(msgHash32: Uint8Array(32), privKey32: Uint8Array(32)) -> Uint8Array(64) [BIP-340]; schnorrVerify(sig: Uint8Array(64), msgHash32: Uint8Array(32), pubKeyX32: Uint8Array(32)) -> boolean (never throws, returns false on malformed input); getPublicKeyX(privKey32) -> Uint8Array(32) x-only pubkey; sha256(bytes: Uint8Array) -> Uint8Array(32); randomPrivateKey() -> Uint8Array(32) (rejection-sampled valid secp256k1 scalar via crypto.getRandomValues); bytesToHex(Uint8Array) -> lowercase hex string; hexToBytes(string) -> Uint8Array. Built from @noble/curves@2.2.0 + @noble/hashes@2.2.0 with `npx esbuild entry.js --bundle --minify --format=esm` (entry source: nostr-lab/entry.js). Requires globalThis.crypto — present in every browser; in Node 18 tests needs --experimental-global-webcrypto.

BUILD+SIGN A NOSTR EVENT:
import { schnorrSign, getPublicKeyX, sha256, randomPrivateKey, bytesToHex, hexToBytes } from './vendor/nostr-crypto.js';
const enc = new TextEncoder();
const sk = randomPrivateKey();                       // or persisted burner from localStorage
const ev = { pubkey: bytesToHex(getPublicKeyX(sk)), created_at: Math.floor(Date.now()/1000), kind: 42, tags: [["e", CHANNEL_ID, "wss://relay.damus.io", "root"]], content: text };
const idBytes = sha256(enc.encode(JSON.stringify([0, ev.pubkey, ev.created_at, ev.kind, ev.tags, ev.content])));
ev.id  = bytesToHex(idBytes);
ev.sig = bytesToHex(schnorrSign(idBytes, sk));
ws.send(JSON.stringify(["EVENT", ev]));

VERIFY AN INCOMING EVENT:
const idBytes = sha256(enc.encode(JSON.stringify([0, e.pubkey, e.created_at, e.kind, e.tags, e.content])));
const valid = bytesToHex(idBytes) === e.id && schnorrVerify(hexToBytes(e.sig), idBytes, hexToBytes(e.pubkey));

EVENT-ID SERIALIZATION RULES (NIP-01, verified byte-for-byte against nostr-tools): id = sha256 over the UTF-8 BYTES (TextEncoder, never UTF-16) of the JSON serialization of the 6-element array [0, pubkey_lowercase_hex, created_at_integer, kind_integer, tags, content]. Native JSON.stringify matches NIP-01 escaping exactly: ONLY double-quote (\"), backslash (\\), and control chars < 0x20 are escaped (\n, \t, \r as two-char forms; other controls as \\uXXXX); all other characters — accented latin, CJK, emoji incl. surrogate pairs — pass through RAW as UTF-8, NOT \\uXXXX-escaped. No whitespace between elements. NEVER hand-concatenate the serialization; JSON.stringify on the array is the spec. Verified: bundle-signed events with content 'unicode ✓ 中文 emoji 🤠 newline\\nquote\"backslash\\\\ tab\\t' pass nostr-tools verifyEvent, and the bundle recomputes nostr-tools-generated ids exactly (12/12 tests PASS in nostr-lab/test-bundle.mjs).
